notes:

THE MAW -- one long approach, one gate, one room that is the whole point.

  1 SPAWN (16,2) facing SOUTH at the head of a causeway. This is the only
    level that opens on a long sightline instead of a wall: five cells wide,
    eleven long, glowing nukage gutters down both flanks and paired metal
    columns ON the path at y4, y7 and y10, so the walk is a slalom through a
    receding colonnade rather than a march down a tube -- and at one cell's
    range those columns are the brightest faces on the approach. At the far
    end, two torch-bright cells
    frame a yellow door. The entire level is legible from the spawn cell.
  2 THE CAUSEWAY (light 4). The safe path is the middle three cells and the
    columns pinch it to one cell three times; the gutters hurt. Nothing stops you walking the whole way down and trying the
    door and being refused. The refusal is the level's first real beat.
  3 Both side branches are entered by stepping INTO nukage: west at (14,8),
    east at (18,11). You cannot explore without paying.
  4 WEST -> THE KEY CHAMBER (x3-8 y5-11, light 4). A glow cell at (2,8) burns
    behind the YELLOW KEY at (4,8), so the key reads from the corridor mouth
    ten cells away. A hulk at (6,9) stands between, in a room with four
    columns and no space to circle comfortably. Hard, on purpose.
  5 EAST -> THE ARMOURY (x24-28 y7-13, light 4). Optional: autogun, armour,
    shells. Symmetric with beat 4, so the player who does both walks into the
    arena kitted and the player who does neither still gets in.
  6 THE GREAT DOOR (16,13) opens onto a single dark cell (16,14), and then --
  7 THE MAW (x9-26 y15-28, light 6). 18x14, the biggest room in ABYSS.
    Twenty-three metal columns on a 3-cell pitch, a 2x2 glowing altar dead
    centre, torches and two barrels. The doorway lands you at (16,15) between
    two columns: the first view is four aisles opening at once.
  8 The MAW waits at (17,25), directly behind the altar, so the boss and the
    landmark are one silhouette -- you always know which way it is.
  9 AMBUSH: the trigger line (15,16)-(17,16) is the three cells you must
    cross to leave the doorway. Sealed panels at x8 and x27 open on the
    flanks and four sleepers -- two hulks, two gunners -- come in from behind
    the column rows. The fight starts with your back to a closed door.
 10 The column grid gives roughly twenty safe pivots instead of four, so the
    boss fight is a running fight. Medkits at (10,22) and (25,22) sit in the
    far corners: healing costs you position. Two barrels flank the altar.
 11 EXIT (16,28)-(17,28) is directly BEHIND the Maw against the south wall,
    with a glow face. The last thing the level asks is that you get PAST it.
end
